From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 22:34:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02447/11362] [outer-loop] offline->live bridge v1 (cross-game
 value head): plumbed, measured, honest null

Operator: build the bridge so offline solves flow through BFS/DFS/router into the
LIVE agent and benefit unseen-game submissions. (Bridge CODE landed in HEAD via a
conductor checkpoint sweep -- arc_competition_agent.py value_head wiring,
arc_cross_game_verifier_train.py 16-game corpus, arc_leaderboard_eval.py explorer_vh
mode, models/arc_verifier_cross_game.json. This commit records the result artifacts +
the honest verdict.)

WHAT WAS BUILT (the flywheel, end-to-end, additive/opt-in -- default agent unchanged):
  offline banked solves (16 games) -> replay frame-only -> cross_game_features +
  steps-to-next-level-up labels (480 states) -> ONE cross-game linear value head
  (models/arc_verifier_cross_game.json) -> loaded by the LIVE StepwiseExplorer ->
  routes its frontier on UNSEEN games -> measured by arc_leaderboard_eval --games oracle.
The trajectories are frame-only-replayable (reproduction-gated), so this is live-legal
training data even though the offline SOLVER read internals. Every future offline solve
retrains the head; the live agent inherits it. That is the offline->live distillation.

MEASURED (frame-only, no banked plan, no GameAdapter; vs the offline oracle's 32 levels):
  baseline explorer (BFS)                 : 8/32
  value head as frontier OVERRIDE         : 3/32  REGRESSION (the 5-feature linear head
        misroutes away from BFS-found shallow wins -- cd82/ls20/m0r0/r11l broke)
  value head as depth-primary TIEBREAK    : 8/32  NEUTRAL (recovers BFS, provably cannot
        regress; the cheap head is inert as a tiebreak)
  E3 world-model induction (gemma-4-12B)  : 0/6 gap-1 games closed (~310s/game; the small
        local model's induced engines never produced a winning plan)

HONEST VERDICT: the bridge architecture is right and now PLUMBED + MEASURABLE, but the
CHEAP instantiations do NOT move the live 8/32. _frontier was fixed to depth-primary
(value as tiebreak) so the wired head can never regress the default agent. The two real
levers the gap points to: (1) a RICHER learned value representation (grid-embedding / TRM,
not 5 linear features); (2) STRONGER world-model induction (bigger model / RFT the
proposer on our banked solves). This null is the point of measuring live honestly --
it stops us believing the cheap bridge works, and aims the next iteration precisely.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
